# Cursor rules — litellm-ingestion-agent

You are working in `litellm-ingestion-agent`, a spec-driven project.

- Source of truth: `docs/SPEC.md`. If code and spec disagree, flag it — do not
  silently change behavior. Propose the spec edit first.
- Data shapes: `docs/EXTRACTION_CONTRACT.md` (human) and
  `src/litellm_ingestion_agent/models.py` (executable). Keep them in sync.
- Build order: `docs/MILESTONES.md`. Work one GitHub issue at a time.
- Standards: `ruff` clean, `pytest` green, new behavior has tests.
- Never write real API keys or secrets into code, tests, or docs. Use
  placeholders like `sk-...` in fixtures.
- Keep functions small, typed, and documented with docstrings.

## GitHub protocol
- One issue = one branch named issue-<n>-<slug>. Comment on the issue when starting.
- PRs include "Closes #<n>" and keep ruff + pytest green.

## Spec change protocol
- Spec (docs/SPEC.md) changes BEFORE code, never after.
- Requirement change → edit spec → append to spec changelog → update affected
  issues (gh issue edit/comment) → new issues for new scope, close dead ones.
- If the spec doesn't cover what the task needs, stop and propose the spec edit.
